==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{root|ang|ine-pro|*h₁lewdʰ-}} {{dercat|ang|ine-pro}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*liud(i)}}, from {{der|ang|gem-pro|*liudiz}}. Closely related to {{m|ang|lēode}} and {{m|ang|lēodan}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
Cognates include {{cog|goh|liut}}, {{cog|non|ljōðr}}, and {{cog|fy|-lju}}; and, outside the Germanic languages, {{cog|lt|liáudis||common people}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*ľudъ}} ({{cog|ru|люд}}). {{rel-bottom}}

